  "title": "P1×3L — Full Collection",
  "summary": "A P1×3L is the atomic unit of digital art, vibrant and alive. Artists choreograph P1×3Ls, and P1×3Ls possess artists. This exhibition brings together Nicolas Sassoon, Francoise Gamma, Andreas Gysin (aka ertdfgcvb), Raquel Meyers, and p1xelfool, artists who foreground the materiality of their digital medium.\n\nRaquel Meyers uses vintage Commodore 64 computers and Teletext systems to create uniform grids of text and symbols, performing these images live. ertdfgcvb crafts generative software works from graphic symbols, focusing on movement and choreography. Francoise Gamma's GIF files explore drawing through jittering lines and smooth movement.",
